{"availability":"available","full":"urchade/GLiNER","name":"GLiNER","description":"Generalist and Lightweight Model for Named Entity Recognition (Extract any entity types from texts)","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":4065,"forks":318,"created":"2023-11-14T18:11:11Z","updated":"2026-10-05T09:06:36Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://urchade.github.io/GLiNER","topics":["information-extraction","large-language-models","named-entity-recognition","natural-language-processing","prompt-tuning"],"demo":"https://urchade.github.io/GLiNER","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:26.702Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:26.702Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:36:26.702Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T22:55:09.834Z","stars":4051,"forks":318},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:36:26.702Z","stars":4065,"forks":318}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Zero-shot NER | Streaming NER | Relation Extraction | PII Detection | Information Extraction | Token Classification","GLiNER is a framework for training and deploying small Named Entity Recognition (NER) models with zero-shot capabilities. In addition to traditional NER, it supports incremental streaming NER, joint entity and relation extraction, and multi-task token classification. GLiNER is fine-tunable, optimized to run on CPUs and consumer hardware, and has performance competitive with LLMs several times its size, like ChatGPT and UniNER.","Other tasks such as text classification, entity linking, and schema extraction are supported through projects in the Ecosystem."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/urchade/GLiNER/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"537e4ec0cfd5975ca367494e8592fa276c006fb3064b9f07105b189a85e8e583","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T22:55:09.959Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T22:55:09.959Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Zero-shot NER | Streaming NER | Relation Extraction | PII Detect